# CODEOWNERS for panakoes
#
# GitHub uses this file to auto-suggest reviewers when a PR touches
# a path. Solo OSS today; this becomes load-bearing the moment a
# second active contributor lands. Pre-positioning it so the structure
# is in place when the team grows.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins. Keep general rules
# at the top, more specific rules below.
#
# Format reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything in this repo.
*                                @Aztec03hub

# Architecture, decisions, and project-shape docs are maintainer-led.
# Listed explicitly so the intent is clear in CODEOWNERS itself, not
# just absorbed into the catch-all above.
/docs/adr/                        @Aztec03hub
/docs/design/                     @Aztec03hub
/docs/architecture.md             @Aztec03hub
/docs/operations/                 @Aztec03hub
/PLANNING.md                      @Aztec03hub
/SCOPE.md                         @Aztec03hub
/CLAUDE.md                        @Aztec03hub

# CI/CD, branch protection, and security policies. Anything in these
# paths affects how every other change ships and gets reviewed; route
# to the maintainer explicitly even when team scale grows.
/.github/                         @Aztec03hub
/.githooks/                       @Aztec03hub
/.gitleaks.toml                   @Aztec03hub
/.gitattributes                   @Aztec03hub
/.pre-commit-config.yaml          @Aztec03hub
/Makefile                         @Aztec03hub
/scripts/                         @Aztec03hub
/SECURITY.md                      @Aztec03hub

# Infrastructure-as-code. Every Terraform change is a production
# blast-radius event; route to the maintainer for review on top of
# any other listed reviewer the future team may add.
/infra/                           @Aztec03hub

